{"subjectId":"python","id":"dataclasses-typing","title":"Dataclasses, Enums & Type Hints","group":"Object-Oriented Python","order":17,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Less boilerplate, clearer intent: <code>@dataclass</code> writes the dull methods for you, <code>Enum</code> names your constants, and type hints document everything.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-wand\"></i>@dataclass</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>from dataclasses import dataclass, field\n\n@dataclass(order=True)\nclass Student:\n    name: str\n    marks: int = 0\n    tags: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)   # never a bare [] default\n\ns = Student(\"Asha\", 91)\nprint(s)                                    # Student(name='Asha', marks=91, tags=[])\nprint(s == Student(\"Asha\", 91))             # True\nprint(sorted([Student(\"b\", 2), Student(\"a\", 5)])[0].name)   # a</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>@dataclass</code></td><td>Generates <code>__init__</code>, <code>__repr__</code>, <code>__eq__</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>order=True</code></td><td>Adds <code>&lt;</code>, <code>&lt;=</code>, <code>&gt;</code>, <code>&gt;=</code> comparing fields in order</td></tr><tr><td><code>frozen=True</code></td><td>Immutable instances (and hashable)</td></tr><tr><td><code>slots=True</code></td><td>Uses <code>__slots__</code> — less memory, faster attribute access (3.10+)</td></tr><tr><td><code>field(default_factory=…)</code></td><td>A fresh mutable default per instance</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-list-numbers\"></i>Enum</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>from enum import Enum, auto\n\nclass Status(Enum):\n    TODO = auto()\n    DONE = auto()\n\ns = Status.DONE\nprint(s, s.name, s.value)              # Status.DONE DONE 2\nprint(Status[\"TODO\"] is Status.TODO)   # True\nprint([m.name for m in Status])        # ['TODO', 'DONE']</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-tag\"></i>Type hints</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>from typing import Optional, TypedDict, Callable\n\ndef find(names: list[str], target: str) -&gt; Optional[int]:\n    return names.index(target) if target in names else None\n\ndef apply(f: Callable[[int], int], x: int) -&gt; int:\n    return f(x)\n\nclass User(TypedDict):\n    id: int\n    email: str\n\nu: User = {\"id\": 1, \"email\": \"a@b.co\"}\nprint(find([\"a\", \"b\"], \"b\"), apply(lambda n: n * 2, 4), u[\"email\"])   # 1 8 a@b.co</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-brackets\"></i>Built-in generics</h3><p><code>list[int]</code>, <code>dict[str, float]</code>, <code>tuple[int, ...]</code> (3.9+).</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrows-join\"></i>Unions</h3><p><code>int | None</code> (3.10+) is the same as <code>Optional[int]</code>.</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-shield-check\"></i>Checked by tools</h3><p>Hints are not enforced at runtime — run <code>mypy</code> or <code>pyright</code> to catch type errors.</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-bulb\"></i>Why bother</h3><p>Better autocomplete, self-documenting signatures, fewer bugs in large code.</p></div></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-database\"></i>__slots__</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>class Point:\n    __slots__ = (\"x\", \"y\")      # no per-instance __dict__\n    def __init__(self, x, y):\n        self.x, self.y = x, y\n\np = Point(1, 2)\ntry:\n    p.z = 3\nexcept AttributeError:\n    print(\"no new attributes\")  # no new attributes</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p><code>__slots__</code> saves memory when you create millions of small objects, at the cost of not being able to add attributes dynamically.</p></div></section>"}